ctually  using the power of sunshine to make her  body large and muscular when she  overuses this power as she did in the  fight against galand and malascula she  reverts back to her original form  overall Gawain has a ton of potential  and the combination of possessing  sunshine and being able to use Advanced  magic could make her one of the  strongest characters in the entire  series at some point in the future she's  almost like what would happen if escanor  and Merlin had a daughter which is  something to think about that said  Gawain still has a long way to go in  order to truly Master the power of  sunshine and she is not even close to  the power level of former Sunshine users  Mile and escanor she also has a lot of  work to do when it comes to disciplining  herself and reigning in her own ego  until she makes some serious  improvements in that regard she'll  remain at number four on our list at  number 3 3 we have the main protagonist  of our story Percival Percival is the  first night of the Apocalypse that we  meet at the very beginning and according  to the prophecy he is the Knight of  death he has a very unique appearance as  his hair is green and shaped like a pair  of wings his eyes are purple and he  looks like a 10 year old kid even though  he's actually 16. he also often wears  his Grandpa's big old helmet a helmet  which is clearly too big for his head  and this adds to the uniqueness of his  appearance Percival was raised by his  grandpa in total isolation from the  outside world atop a Giant pillar-shaped  Mountain percival's grandpa is actually  a former Holy Knight of Camelot and he  spent countless hours training a young  person to become a powerful Warrior this  training started when Percival was only  three years old and it ended when  percival's father Ironside another Holy  Night of Camelot suddenly showed up and  killed the percival's grandfather after  that person possible set out on a  journey to avenge his grandpa and so his  isolation from the outside world came to  an abrupt and as Percival Ventures into  the outside world and begins to interact  with other people he slowly begins to  discover and develop his unique magical  abilities Percival possesses a lot more  strength and durability than an ordinary  human in addition Percival seems to have  enhanced resistance against drugs and  other types of potions and he has above  average lung capacity due in part to the  fact that he grew up at a very high  altitude on top of his impressive  physical skills and combat capabilities  things that he developed through many  years of training with his grandpa  Percival also discovers that he  possesses a very rare and unique type of  magic called hope hope is Magic that is  powered by the hope of the user's allies  and by the faith that the Allies place  in the user you know those memes about  the power of friendship in anime and  manga well this is literally that  pellegard believes that hope is an  extremely rare type of magic known as  hero type magic which manifests in only  a very small number of people hope magic  enables Percival to generate a magical  Aura around his body or parts of his  body and he can then manipulate that  aura in a variety of different ways for  example the magical Aura allows him to  defend himself by acting as his shield  and reducing the damage from enemy  attacks it also enhances his own  physical strength when he is the one  doing the attacking and it can even heal  a life-threatening injuries almost  instantly the aura can also assume  different shapes and forms such as  turning itself into a pair of wings and  allowing Percival to literally fly on  top of that Holt magic can absorb the  magic attacks of others and shoot them  back at the attacker and Percival is  also able to use hope magic to create a  bunch of Chibi clones these chibi clones  have a will of their own and they assist  Percival whenever he finds himself in a  tough spot the Clones also have the  ability to heal percival's injuries and  the injuries of his allies and as  powerful and versatile as all of these  magic powers are we're not even done yet  there is still more to percival's powers  and abilities for example he possesses  the ability to instantly drain all the  fluid out of a living being just by  touching the person directly basically  mummifying that part of the person's  body that Percival had come into direct  contact with Percival first demonstrated  this ability when he was in a state of  extraordinary agitation and despair as  he falsely believed that his friends had  just been killed normal healing magic  cannot even reverse the effects of this  strange mummification not even goddess  healing magic can reverse it and so only  percival's own hope magic seems capable  of reversing its effects interestingly  enough Percival is able to speak the  language of demon although no one seems  to know why not even Percival we still  don't know who percival's mother is by  the way and this might be a hint that  Percival may not be just an ordinary  human and that he may be of mixed race  Heritage like maybe he is part demon  we'll have to wait and see anyway  Percival currently possesses the  legendary sword Dragon handle which once  belonged to meliodas Dragon handle is  also one part of the coffin of Eternal  darkness which is something we learned  back in the original Seven Deadly Sins  Series this once Broken Sword was  repaired and turned into a fully  functioning sword by Hauser and Percival  has now learned to use hope magic to  enhance the power of the sword as the  main character in the story and the guy  with literally the power of Friendship  on his side Percival has the most  potential out of anyone to become the  strongest character in the entire manga  but at this point in time he still lacks  experience as a holy night and he is  still learning to understand and control  his magic while Percival still has more  self-control than Gawain does and for  that reason he would probably defeat her  in battle he still doesn't have the  combat experience and Technical skill  that Tristan and Lancelot possess and  for that reason he remains at number  three on our list at number two we have  the son of meliodas and Elizabeth and  the prophesies the Knight of pestilence  Prince Tristan when he appears in  chapter 54 of the sequel manga Tristan  is already an experienced holy Knight  and he has a platoon of holy nights  under his command this platoon has a  very original name by the way the  Tristan platoon we know that Tristan has  been exceptionally strong and skilled in  combat ever since he was a child and  what really makes him unique is the fact  that he inherited both goddess and demon  powers from his parents this makes him a  special kind of creature in the world of  the seven deadly sins and its sequel on  Nephilim Tristan is even able to  manifest both demon and goddess Powers  at the same time which is something that  we haven't seen since the days of my l  slash Esther Rosa and even then Tristan  is still different because unlike mael  Tristan is literally the child of one of  the strongest demons and one of the  strongest goddesses in history it's  interesting to note that Tristan uses  two swords in battle one sword is black  and the other is white in one of the  question Corners author nakabasuzuki  revealed that Tristan's two swords are  actually named mael and Esther Rosa  Tristan has access to goddess magic such  as summoning large angelic wings that  allow him to fly using unbelievably  powerful healing abilities and using  other standard goddess powers like Ark  most of the time Tristan prefers to rely  on his goddess Powers alone but when he  is pushed to the point where he can't  win by using only goddess powers he is  able to tap into his demon side when he  Taps into his demonic Powers Tristan's  eyes turned black and a large demon Mark  appears on his forehead this demon mode  makes Tristan a lot more powerful but  it's also much harder to turn off and to  control in this form Tristan kind of  goes berserk and he makes rash and risky  decisions that he would not have made  otherwise for example demon mode Tristan  tries to fight King Arthur head on  despite clear warnings that he still  isn't strong enough to defeat him and  then Tristan's father meliodas is forced  to intervene and risk his own life in  order to protect his son from Arthur I  believe that Tristan and his demon mode  is clearly stronger than Percival and  Gawain at this point in time for example  once he awakens his demon mode Tristan  is able to easily destroy the fusion of  melascula and galand even though no one  on the battlefield was able to do any  significant damage to them before that  and that includes Percival and going but  it is clear that Tristan still hasn't  mastered his demon mode and that he has  a long way to go before he reaches his  full potential in fact he actively  avoids using his demon mode because he  knows that he can't control it and he  knows that this mode makes him act out  in ways that are both abnormal and  dangerous  because he is the son of one of the  strongest goddesses and one of the  strongest demons in history and because  he possesses the ability to use both  demon and goddess Powers at the same  time Tristan has absolutely incredible  potential and he is definitely a  contender for becoming one of the  strongest characters in the entire  series at some point in the future but  for now we know that he isn't the  strongest Knight of the Apocalypse  because Tristan himself confirms it in  chapter 80 of the manga speaking  directly to Percival Tristan says that  he and Lancelot were evenly matched in  power until about six years ago that is  when Lancelot mysteriously disappeared  from the kingdom of benwick when he  returned three years later he seemed  fine as if nothing had happened but  there was one massive change in Lancelot  he had somehow attained a terrifying new  strength and magical power and  lancelot's strength is currently already  on are with the legendary seven deadly  sins from the original manga Tristan  openly admits that lancelot's power is  far beyond his own and so it's time to  talk about the strongest Knight of the  Apocalypse the son of Bonn and Elaine  Lancelot Lancelot is the night of War  according to the prophecy and because he  is half fairy he has the unique ability  to shapeshift Lancelot has actually been  around since like chapter 2 of the  sequel manga but we didn't realize at  first that it was him because all the  way up to chapter 47 he was taking the  form of a talking Fox named sin if you  were a fan of the original Seven Deadly  Sins which I would assume that most of  us are then you know that Lancelot was  first introduced in chapter  346.5 of the original manga that chapter  tells the story of how at the age of 10  Lancelot and his trainer Jericho  disappeared from benwick as a result of  Strange Magic magic that is probably  related to the Lady of the Lake because  spoiler alert nakaba borrows a lot from  Arthurian Legend and in Arthurian Legend  Lancelot spends several years being  raised by the Lady of the Lake as we  learned from Tristan Lancelot went  missing six years ago and he was missing  for three years but then he returned as  if nothing happened except he was  suddenly a lot more powerful and I am  willing to bet that this power-up is  linked to the Lady of the Lake in some  way but let's move on when he finally  reveals his true identity in the Four  Knights of the Apocalypse manga Lancelot  explains to Percival and the others that  he is actually in the service of  meliodas the king of Leones Lancelot is  basically a secret agent working  directly for meliodas and his mission is  to locate all the Knights of the  apocalypse and bring them to leonis  where they will meet the king the more  we learn about Lancelot the more we  realize just how incredibly strong and  skilled away Warrior he is and yet  despite this most people have no idea  who he is they haven't even heard any  rumors about him despite the fact that  he is such a strong Warrior who happens  to only be 16 years of age and that is  something that people would certainly  want to talk about but the reason why  there are no rumors about Lancelot is  because he makes sure that none of the  enemies who face him in battle will ever  live to tell the tale he straight up  eliminates all of his enemies after  defeating them which is pretty ruthless  but it is also incredibly useful in his  line of work after all he is essentially  a secret agent who operates in the  shadows using many different forms and  identities then if people start talking  about him and he becomes famous then he  would no longer be able to carry out his  important missions we know that even as  a 10 year old kid Lancelot had above  average physical strength Superior  reflexes and exceptional combat  capabilities as I mentioned earlier his  power used to be on par with Tristan and  then he disappeared and came back much  stronger along with the ability to  shapeshift lancelot's connection to the  fairy Clan also gives him the ability to  read the minds of his opponents which is  a power known as heart reading this  ability is extremely useful in battle  because it allows Lancelot to anticipate  his opponent's next move and since his  opponents usually don't know anything  about him having a connection to the  fairy Clan lancelot's ability to read  them usually catches them completely off  guard in addition Lancelot is also very  skilled Archer and he uses a bow and  arrow with unbelievable speed and  accuracy his offensive capabilities are  absolutely devastating and we saw this  early on as he was able to instantly  kill doronak one of the Holy Knights of  Camelot with just one punch to the gut  and if that wasn't enough Lancelot has a  magical ability called shining road  which allows him to fire a beam of light  at an opponent this beam will then chase  after its Target and follow it like a  heat-seeking missile until it destroys  it  lancelot's true power becomes apparent  in chapter 79 when he takes on King  Arthur one on one and this is after  Arthur already outclassed Tristan and  after he even managed to gain the upper  hand on meliodas although to be fair  meliodas was being held back by the fact  that he was protecting his out of  control son Lancelot ends up intervening  to stop meliodas from being killed by  Arthur and then he goes toe-to-toe with  Arthur himself Lancelot actually lands  several powerful blows on Arthur causing  Serious injury and forcing Arthur to  activate the power of Chaos in order to  regenerate although I guess technically  the power of chaos activates itself when  it senses that its host is in danger so  Arthur doesn't even have to do anything  consciously chaos instinctively acts to  protect him at this point Arthur  confirms that meliodas at full power is  still stronger than Lancelot but there  is no doubt that Lancelot is the strong  longest of the Four Knights of the  Apocalypse at least for now in fact  meliodas and Tristan seemed hopeful that  even with the power of chaos actively  protecting Arthur Lancelot may still  have a chance to defeat him I mean that  is just an incredible level of  confidence that meliodas and Tristan  have in lancelot's power but before  Lancelot can force a Battle to the death  with Arthur the holy Knights of Camelot  arrive on the scene inside like a flying  monster ship that appears in the sky  above leonis Arthur then warps up to the  ship and the ship disappears before  Lancelot and the others can stop them  but as he departs Arthur declares  all-out war and he vows to hunt down the  Four Knights of the apocalypse and their  allies and to eradicate them all that is  pretty intense and there we have it the  Four Knights of the Apocalypse ranked  from weakest to strongest based on all  the information that we have thus far  all four of them have rare and unique  powers and incredible potential and it  is possible that these rankings might  shift sometime in the near future  personally I was surprised to learn that  Lancelot was already on the level of the  legendary seven deadly sins from the  original manga especially since we know  that he's only a 16 year old kid but  that also makes things more interesting  since Lancelot proves that we won't have  to wait hundreds of chapters for the  Four Knights of the Apocalypse to reach  the level that the seven deadly sins  were at at the end of the original manga  things are moving very quickly in the  sequel and we can expect the action to  intensify now that King Arthur has  declared all-out war against the Four  Knights of the Apocalypse the Four  Knights are now assembled the battle  lines have been drawn and I can't wait  to see what happens next I'm especially  interested to see the other sins return  to the story including of course Bon  Diane and King based on recent events  and clues in the latest chapters we can  expect all of them to appear soon which  is awesome let me know what you guys  think do you agree with my rankings and  if not where would you place the Four  Knights in terms of current strength and  power level where do you think the story  is going to go from here don't forget to  comment down below I always love hearing  from you if you enjoyed this video and  you want to see more seven deadly sins  and Four Knights of the Apocalypse  content here on the channel leave a  quick like to help me out with that  YouTube algorithm and if you haven't  taken the time to subscribe yet do me a  big favor and make this the video that  you subscribe and hit that notification  Bell to turn on all notifications if you  don't do that you're still gonna miss a  ton of our videos in the future even if  you are subscribed it's just how YouTube  works you can also hit me up on Twitter  and